  "problem": "Let $z$ be a $6$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{2}={z}^{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{6} & =({z}^{6})^{3} \\\\  & =(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement I, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{3})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
